  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures the Mountain Goats performing at Turner Hall in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, on April 10, 2024 [1][3]. The audio is a matrix mix that combines the soundboard with audience microphones, offering a balanced perspective on the live event [1]. The setlist features a diverse range of material, including the rare tracks \"Azo Tle Nelli In Tlalticpac\" and \"Extraction Point,\" which are among the less frequently archived songs in the band's history [1]. The performance also includes the first archived recordings of \"From the Nebraska Plant,\" \"Bell Swamp Connection,\" and \"Only Takes a Few,\" making this a significant entry in the archive's collection [1]. The show is the 416th of 467 archived performances for the band, following a previous show at the Aladdin Theater in March 2024 [2]. The recording was captured using high-quality equipment, including a Zoom f3 and Rode NT-SF1 ambisonic microphone, and processed to enhance clarity [1]. The taper notes express gratitude to the sound engineer, band, and venue staff for a fun night [1]. The poster for the event is credited to Discotech [3]. This matrix recording is the only available capture of this specific show, documenting the full 22-song set [1].",
